---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="A little about vergil1000, the person behind the projects, words, experiments, and occasional rabbit holes."
	pubDate={new Date('November 16 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<h2>Hey, I'm vergil1000.</h2>

	<p>
		That's what I go by around here. I'm currently pursuing
		my M.Tech in Applied Mechanics at IIT Delhi, having
		studied Mechanical Engineering for my undergraduate degree.
	</p>

	<p>
		But academics are only one small part of what occupies
	my time. I've never been particularly good at sticking
		to one interest. I like learning new things, making
		things, and occasionally getting carried away by an
		idea that leads me somewhere entirely unexpected.
	</p>

	<h2>Making things</h2>

	<p>
		I enjoy programming and development, particularly building
		things for the web. I've worked on websites, applications,
		automation scripts, and various little experiments.
	</p>

	<p>
		I like taking an idea, figuring out how to approach it,
		and eventually turning it into something tangible.
		Sometimes it works beautifully; sometimes it turns
		into a debugging session that lasts considerably longer
		than anticipated.
	</p>

	<p>
		I'm also interested in design, visual communication,
		and content creation. I enjoy playing around with ideas,
		presentation, storytelling, and finding interesting
		ways to communicate something.
	</p>

	<h2>Words and music</h2>

	<p>
		I write poetry occasionally. Usually, it's an attempt
		to capture a thought or feeling that doesn't quite
		translate into ordinary conversation.
	</p>

	<p>
		I like ambiguity, imagery, things left unsaid, and
		the different interpretations a few carefully chosen
		words can invite. I don't follow any particular style
	or schedule. I just write when something makes me want to.
	</p>

	<p>
		Music is another constant. I'm learning to sing and
	experimenting with my voice, trying to develop both
	technical control and emotional expression.
	</p>

	<p>
		I'm particularly drawn to Chester Bennington's intensity
		and Arijit Singh's expressiveness. Very different artists,
	but both inspire different aspects of what I'd like to
	develop as a singer.
	</p>

	<h2>The physical side</h2>

	<p>
		I'm quite invested in strength training, calisthenics,
		and gymnastics. Beyond just getting stronger, I'm
		interested in learning skills that demand strength,
		coordination, mobility, and body control.
	</p>

	<p>
		Handstands, muscle-ups, levers, bar work, and various
		gymnastics movements are things I enjoy working towards.
		There's something satisfying about chasing a movement
		you can't quite do yet, gradually getting closer,
		and eventually making it your own.
	</p>

	<p>
		There's always another skill to learn, another limitation
		to work around, and another reason to get back to training.
	</p>

	<h2>Curiosity and everything else</h2>

	<p>
		My interests extend well beyond these things. Technology,
		artificial intelligence, mathematics, financial markets,
	science, psychology, and plenty of other subjects have
		all sent me down their respective rabbit holes.
	</p>

	<p>
		I don't necessarily intend to turn every interest into
	a career or a productive pursuit. Sometimes being curious
	is reason enough.
	</p>

	<h2>Why this website?</h2>

	<p>
		Mostly, I wanted a place of my own.
	</p>

	<p>
		A place to collect things I've made, things I've written,
		things I've learned, and things I don't want to lose
		to the endless scroll of social media.
	</p>

	<p>
		I don't want everything here to be an achievement,
	a milestone, or a carefully curated showcase. Some things
	might be unfinished, some might be experiments, and some
	might simply exist because I felt like making them.
	</p>

	<p>
		Think of this as an evolving archive of my interests,
		creations, thoughts, and occasional obsessions.
	</p>

	<p>
		There's no particular direction I'm trying to take
	it. We'll see where it goes.
	</p>

	<p>
		Thanks for stopping by.
	</p>
</Layout>
